},{type:"modal-page",path:"/modals/:uid"},{type:"pressHome",path:"/press"},{type:"press",path:"/press/:uid"},{type:"blogHome",path:"/news"},{type:"blog",path:"/news/:uid"},{type:"faq-page",path:"/faqs/:subpath2?/:uid",resolvers:{subpath2:"subpath2"}},{type:"landing-page",path:"/:uid"},{type:"content-page",path:"/:subpath1?/:subpath2?/:uid",resolvers:{subpath1:"subpath1",subpath2:"subpath2"}}]},preview:"/preview",toolbar:true,imports:["vue"],components:{richTextComponents:"~/prismic/richTextComponents"}}},app:{baseURL:"/",buildId:"7e544b5a-0a75-4bc7-b691-fdfd0ac7333b",buildAssetsDir:"/_nuxt/",cdnURL:""}}</script><script type="application/json" data-nuxt-data="nuxt-app" data-ssr="true" id="__NUXT_DATA__">[["ShallowReactive",1],{"prerenderedAt":2,"data":3,"state":258,"once":13562,"_errors":13563,"serverRendered":90,"path":13565,"pinia":13566},1784019875794,["ShallowReactive",4],{"content-page-subpath1:how-to-send-a-bike":5,"page-header-video-undefined":43},{"uid":6,"document":7,"postSlices":257},"how-to-send-a-bike",{"titleTag":8,"metaDescription":9,"canonical":10,"subpath1":11,"subpath2":22,"slices":23},"How to Send a Bike with a Courier | Evri Cheap & Fast Delivery","For such a large and fragile item, shipping a bike can seem like a daunting task, so in this guide, we show you the easiest way to send a bike by post.","how-to-send-a-bike.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fhow-to-send-a-bike",{"id":12,"type":13,"tags":14,"lang":16,"slug":17,"first_publication_date":18,"last_publication_date":18,"uid":17,"link_type":19,"key":20,"isBroken":21},"ZL-1EREAACAAEkhR","subpath1",[15],"Guides","en-gb","guides","2023-07-25T12:59:36+0000","Document","dd37541c-cb36-4c7d-8c2e-5b2a7ba56a7f",false,{"link_type":19},[24,44,82,129,204],{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":27,"primary":29,"id":41,"slice_type":42,"slice_label":43},"pageHeaderNoCta","sktwi1xtmkfgx8626",[28],{},{"theme":30,"PageHeaderTitle":31,"PageHeaderText":32,"PageHeaderImage":38,"heroImage":39,"videoContent":40,"showPremiumLogo":21},"standard","How to send a bike",[33],{"type":34,"text":35,"spans":36,"direction":37},"paragraph","Learn how to safely and securely package a bike ready to be sent with a courier",[],"ltr",{},{},{"link_type":19},"page_header$759e58e5-5ec1-46f1-910a-011c67e413a6","page_header",null,{"variation":45,"version":26,"items":46,"primary":47,"id":80,"slice_type":81,"slice_label":43},"default-slice",[],{"CardImage":48,"CardAvatar":59,"CardTitle":60,"CardText":61,"ButtonText":68,"ButtonUrl":69,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":49,"alt":52,"copyright":43,"url":53,"id":54,"edit":55},{"width":50,"height":51},1000,667,"A female Evri van driver poses in front of her blue Evri van.","how-to-send-a-bike.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6zBX5bqstJ9-iO1_EVRI_LOCATION_06_9828.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6zBX5bqstJ9-iO1",{"x":56,"y":56,"zoom":57,"background":58},0,1,"transparent","none","Learn how to package your bike correctly for cheap shipping",[62,65],{"type":34,"text":63,"spans":64,"direction":37},"With more support on the roads for cyclists around the country, the demand for sending a second-hand bike in the post is only growing. But how does one go about sending a bike? Due to a bikes size and fragility, it’s a bit more complicated than simply boxing it up and shipping it out. Adequate preparation must be taken to ensure that the bike can be delivered safely and efficiently without breaking the bank. ",[],{"type":34,"text":66,"spans":67,"direction":37},"In this guide we will cover all of the steps required to post a bike, from preparation and disassembly, all the way through to boxing up and handing it over to one of our couriers. If you’re already confident that you have a bike ready to ship, then you can head straight to sending a parcel with Evri.",[],"Send a bike with a courier",{"id":70,"type":71,"tags":72,"lang":16,"slug":74,"first_publication_date":75,"last_publication_date":76,"uid":77,"url":78,"link_type":19,"key":79,"isBroken":21},"YiX9JBIAACsAFthQ","landing-page",[73],"Send a Parcel","why-send-a-parcel-with-evri","2022-03-07T12:41:12+0000","2026-07-09T13:59:25+0000","send","\u002Fsend","d33de715-15a8-4e0b-9eb5-804cde67191d","card$f8361ea3-6e8a-4234-bc61-d7098b8e89a7","card",{"variation":45,"version":26,"items":83,"primary":125,"id":127,"slice_type":128,"slice_label":43},[84,93,101,109,117],{"title":85,"content":86,"isNumbered":90,"icon":91,"image":92},"Give it a clean",[87],{"type":34,"text":88,"spans":89,"direction":37},"Any abrasion on the surface of the bike could lead to scratches and knicks during the transit process, so it’s important to remove any dirt, mud or debris from the tyres, frame and handlebars. You can do this simply with some warm water and a sponge – just be sure to be extra careful around the finer components of the bike such as the wheel hub or around the chain mechanism. Pat the bike dry once this is completed to avoid any water damage to the packaging materials.",[],true,{},{},{"title":94,"content":95,"isNumbered":90,"icon":99,"image":100},"Remove the saddle and pedals",[96],{"type":34,"text":97,"spans":98,"direction":37},"With a basic set of tools, you can unscrew and remove both the saddle and both of the pedals to be packaged alongside the rest of the bike, so that they don’t protrude beyond the frame requiring an unnecessarily large box. Wrap these in bubble wrap so that any potential movement within the box doesn’t result in any damage.",[],{},{},{"title":102,"content":103,"isNumbered":90,"icon":107,"image":108},"Remove the front wheel",[104],{"type":34,"text":105,"spans":106,"direction":37},"First the brake must be released at the top of the wheel using a lever. For the wheel itself, some bikes are equipped with a simple quick release switch to easily detach the front wheel from its axel; if this isn’t the case, then your tools should make quick work of it anyways. The front wheel can then be packaged alongside the frame in the box, reducing the size of the box required considerably.",[],{},{},{"title":110,"content":111,"isNumbered":90,"icon":115,"image":116},"Turn the handlebar sideways",[112],{"type":34,"text":113,"spans":114,"direction":37},"Now that the wheel has been removed, the handlebars can be turned sideways so that they run parallel to the frame, again reducing the space required within the box by removing protruding components. In some cases, an allen key may be required to loosen the stem, but an advantage of this is that once they have been repositioned, you can tighten the stem once again and it will be fixed in place.",[],{},{},{"title":118,"content":119,"isNumbered":90,"icon":123,"image":124},"Secure the loose parts",[120],{"type":34,"text":121,"spans":122,"direction":37},"You will likely find yourself with a number of screws and other loose parts that will need to be reassembled upon the bike reaching its destination. The best option for ensuring that these parts aren’t lost or bouncing around in the packaging, is to place them in a small plastic bag and fasten them to the frame with tape. Be sure not to place anywhere that would run the risk of chipping or peeling the paint, or alternatively use a tape that is safe to use on paintwork. Similarly, loose effects such as the brake wires will need to be fastened to the frame as well.",[],{},{},{"theme":30,"title":126,"description":43,"showPaddingTop":21},"How to prepare your bike for shipping","list_block$a829ad02-c69d-4691-ad9f-179c754795ec","list_block",{"variation":45,"version":26,"items":130,"primary":201,"id":203,"slice_type":128,"slice_label":43},[131,139,157,165,173],{"title":132,"content":133,"isNumbered":90,"icon":137,"image":138},"Protect frame and protruding parts",[134],{"type":34,"text":135,"spans":136,"direction":37},"For added security inside the box, cover the frame and any protruding parts of the bike with bubble wrap or a similar padding, then secure with tape. This will prevent any scratches or dents during transit.",[],{},{},{"title":140,"content":141,"isNumbered":90,"icon":155,"image":156},"Place inside a sturdy box",[142],{"type":34,"text":143,"spans":144,"direction":37},"You will want to find a box that is only slightly bigger than the size of your bike. We will always suggest looking towards sustainable options, such as reused cardboard, however due to the delicate and specialist nature of sending a bike, it might be advisable to seek out a box designed specifically to house a bike for shipping. These should also possess the necessary sturdiness to keep the bike safe throughout its journey. To make sure your parcel size is suitable for our network, add together the 2 shortest sides and multiply it by 2. Add the length. If the total is less than 245cm, and the longest side is less than 120cm, you’re good to go! Check our size and weight guide for more information.",[145,153],{"start":146,"end":147,"type":148,"data":149},663,684,"hyperlink",{"link_type":150,"url":151,"target":152},"Web","\u002Fsend\u002Fparcel-size-and-weight-guide","_blank",{"start":146,"end":147,"type":154},"strong",{},{},{"title":158,"content":159,"isNumbered":90,"icon":163,"image":164},"Pad out the empty space",[160],{"type":34,"text":161,"spans":162,"direction":37},"Once the bike has been carefully placed inside the box, you will want to pad out the empty space with a soft and light material. For a sustainable solution, we would look towards packing paper, or compostable packing peanuts. These will provide the necessary padding to keep any parts from moving around in the box, reducing the risk of damage.",[],{},{},{"title":166,"content":167,"isNumbered":90,"icon":171,"image":172},"Seal the box",[168],{"type":34,"text":169,"spans":170,"direction":37},"After all of the above steps have been completed, place a piece of paper inside the box with your name, address and phone number, as well as the name and address of the parcels destination so we can complete the parcels journey under any circumstances. Finally, secure the box with an adequate amount of tape, ensuring that no edges are uncovered, and all openings are sealed. Weigh your parcel to check it falls within our maximum weight limit of 15kg - this should include the vast majority of non-electric bicycle models.",[],{},{},{"title":174,"content":175,"isNumbered":21,"icon":193,"image":200},"You’re ready to send!",[176],{"type":34,"text":177,"spans":178,"direction":37},"Now you’ve got your secure parcel, you can book a drop off at one of our 9,000+ ParcelShops or arrange a courier collection to get your bike on the move! Send a bike with a courier today.",[179,185,186,191],{"start":180,"end":181,"type":148,"data":182},73,91,{"link_type":150,"url":183,"target":184},"how-to-send-a-bike.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Ffind-a-parcelshop","_self",{"start":180,"end":181,"type":154},{"start":187,"end":188,"type":148,"data":189},154,186,{"id":70,"type":71,"tags":190,"lang":16,"slug":74,"first_publication_date":75,"last_publication_date":76,"uid":77,"url":78,"link_type":19,"isBroken":21},[73],{"start":187,"end":192,"type":154},187,{"dimensions":194,"alt":196,"copyright":43,"url":197,"id":198,"edit":199},{"width":195,"height":195},40,"Above and beyond icon","how-to-send-a-bike.html\u002F\u002Fev-mercury.cdn.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002F41bf8079-3dd8-48b6-ad6b-013e68421339_above_and_beyond.svg","YflBvREAACIA8pXG",{"x":56,"y":56,"zoom":57,"background":58},{},{"theme":30,"title":202,"description":43,"showPaddingTop":21},"How to package the different parts of your bike","list_block$697c40bc-319e-4915-948c-2fd596cd20d0",{"variation":45,"version":26,"items":205,"primary":253,"id":255,"slice_type":256,"slice_label":43},[206,212,241],{"questionTitle":207,"questionBody":208},"How much does it cost to send a bike with a courier?",[209],{"type":34,"text":210,"spans":211,"direction":37},"You can send a bike with Evri for as little as £6.26, depending on the weight of your bike. So, make sure to get an accurate weight measurement before you book so you don’t spend any more than you have to when shipping with Evri. We also offer next day delivery & courier collection upgrades to make your experience as quick and hassle-free as possible.",[],{"questionTitle":213,"questionBody":214},"Can I send my bike abroad?",[215,224],{"type":34,"text":216,"spans":217,"direction":37},"At Evri we deliver parcels to 200+ countries and territories, meaning our couriers can get your bike almost anywhere in the world. Just be extra careful when packaging your bike to ensure that it is as small as possible, because we do operate with volumetric weight banding for larger parcels which could affect your price. Check out our international prices.",[218,223],{"start":219,"end":220,"type":148,"data":221},324,359,{"link_type":150,"url":222,"target":184},"how-to-send-a-bike.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Finternational-prices",{"start":219,"end":220,"type":154},{"type":34,"text":225,"spans":226,"direction":37},"Save money sending a parcel abroad when you use our international courier service. ",[227,240],{"start":228,"end":229,"type":148,"data":230},52,81,{"id":231,"type":232,"tags":233,"lang":16,"slug":235,"first_publication_date":236,"last_publication_date":237,"uid":238,"url":239,"link_type":19,"isBroken":21},"Yo-FCRIAACUAPA2j","content-page",[234],"International","how-to-send-internationally-with-evri","2022-08-02T10:49:21+0000","2026-03-17T10:29:26+0000","international-courier-services","\u002Four-services\u002Finternational-courier-services",{"start":228,"end":229,"type":154},{"questionTitle":242,"questionBody":243},"Are bikes eligible for compensation?",[244],{"type":34,"text":245,"spans":246,"direction":37},"Evri parcels include free compensation up to £20, however, a bike is most likely going to be far more valuable. Thankfully we are able to offer extended compensation for parcels up to the value of £999 which will cover a wide range of models. Purchase cover for your bike today for absolute peace of mind. Send your bike securely with Evri ",[247,252],{"start":248,"end":249,"type":148,"data":250},306,340,{"id":70,"type":71,"tags":251,"lang":16,"slug":74,"first_publication_date":75,"last_publication_date":76,"uid":77,"url":78,"link_type":19,"isBroken":21},[73],{"start":248,"end":249,"type":154},{"title":254},"Frequently Asked Questions","frequently_asked_questions$e63942d9-8400-453e-8b49-5738d5a991c0","frequently_asked_questions",[24,44,82,129,204],["Reactive",259],{"$sglobal-feature-switches":260,"$sclients":325,"$sglobal-basket-count":43},{"abtasty":261,"accessibe":264,"appPromoBanner":267,"autoDivertUpdates":270,"awin":273,"bulkInternational":276,"bulkSendEnabled":279,"businessAccountForm75Enabled":282,"enableBasketCount":285,"enableBulkPhaseTwo":288,"euCustomsDuty":291,"groovyAdvert":294,"newInternationalSendFlow":297,"newinternationalpages":303,"oohPreferenceFlag":307,"opentel":310,"premium":313,"savedCards":316,"smallParcelSize":319,"yourPricesDrawer":322},{"_createdAt":262,"_updatedAt":263,"enabled":90},"2025-11-05T15:39:37.217Z","2025-11-05T15:39:37.452Z",{"_createdAt":265,"_updatedAt":266,"enabled":90},"2025-07-15T08:41:16.873Z","2025-10-28T11:52:03.675Z",{"_createdAt":268,"_updatedAt":269,"enabled":21},"2026-03-06T12:16:35.816Z","2026-03-06T12:16:36.662Z",{"_createdAt":271,"_updatedAt":272,"enabled":21},"2026-04-30T13:26:45.107Z","2026-04-30T13:26:45.355Z",{"_createdAt":274,"_updatedAt":275,"enabled":21},"2025-08-19T09:46:14.552Z","2025-09-02T10:23:26.022Z",{"_createdAt":277,"_updatedAt":278,"enabled":90},"2025-06-23T14:37:21.102Z","2026-01-28T10:04:13.631Z",{"_createdAt":280,"_updatedAt":281,"enabled":90},"2024-11-14T16:08:24.373Z","2025-06-05T12:32:29.563Z",{"_createdAt":283,"_updatedAt":284,"enabled":90},"2024-11-14T16:09:05.362Z","2024-11-21T10:37:32.927Z",{"_createdAt":286,"_updatedAt":287,"enabled":90},"2025-10-28T13:17:38.716Z","2026-04-14T10:49:05.879Z",{"_createdAt":289,"_updatedAt":290,"enabled":90},"2025-11-07T14:21:27.204Z","2026-05-14T12:54:05.701Z",{"_creat